    "source_record_id": "raw_html_c76170ec1afd4bc1",
    "udare_article_path": "C:\\Users\\HP\\Documents\\LinkCraftor\\backend\\server\\data\\udare_store\\ws_whattoexpect_com\\articles\\first-year-health-and-safety-nine-month-well-baby-visit_c76170ec.html",
    "udare_article_sha256": "1cd9428d7a05353b81232ba11fd41394ce1fc8c41153d7ecdda0e7d4c9b24cd3"
  },
  "source_name": "https://www.whattoexpect.com/first-year/health-and-safety/nine-month-well-baby-visit/",
  "source_type": "website",
  "structure": {
    "block_count": 36,
    "blocks": [
      {
        "block_id": "block_000000",
        "block_index": 0,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h1",
        "text": "The 9-Month Well-Baby Visit",
        "text_sha256": "658432cf6115536bb8c47313c9ded3962cc9f48b4148223457571241f5ba4f73",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000001",
        "block_index": 1,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "NIne Month Well Baby",
        "text_sha256": "37f07b954613e418d6ebb7db0ef96d86a99dc0aa851c681d5bc06117d0ed9eac",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000002",
        "block_index": 2,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Here's what will happen at the 9-month well-baby visit, including the physical checkup, developmental milestones and shots.",
        "text_sha256": "c38530988987b758cae1d4f4997d6429fe02bea31ba90df526fb5de7564b5ef6",
        "word_count": 17
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000003",
        "block_index": 3,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "By now, it might seem like your little genius is picking up a new skill every day. Is that adorable baby babble starting to sound more and more like words? Words you really love to hear, like \"Dada\" or \"Mama\"?",
        "text_sha256": "25588c99904c729730942dc3aae26bff6853e6c7d15c8186068294b06def2c64",
        "word_count": 40
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000004",
        "block_index": 4,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "It’s hard to know whether she’s saying those wonderful words with meaning yet, but really, does it matter when they sound so heart-meltingly sweet?",
        "text_sha256": "552432b1888f09b9f419533c62f20428cf80aaaa98fcd9280671add63c0d1f50",
        "word_count": 24
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000005",
        "block_index": 5,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Also music to your ears: At the 9-month visit, there will be no shots, unless your baby needs to catch up on a previously missed dose or get her annual flu shot. But there will be plenty to cover as the doctor tracks your child's growth and development!",
        "text_sha256": "867ae214dc6b5d170b6f6a9b54cd4f47f9c573102964d7e38bb151e0699e6d85",
        "word_count": 48
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000006",
        "block_index": 6,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "The physical checkup",
        "text_sha256": "ec2df68f3db858cda4725fb37f32d51674754cb5af1274b4c7c0735b5ea5b0e0",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000007",
        "block_index": 7,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "The doctor will once again complete a full physical examination and see how your little one is measuring up. There may also be a routine finger stick to test for anemia, though this may be done later at her 1-year visit instead.",
        "text_sha256": "be8a4646b656611b15593ce995a15e282ed62228f1445efb8dd8676ffd159ea8",
        "word_count": 42
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000008",
        "block_index": 8,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Developmental milestones",
        "text_sha256": "676c4fbf4c110b68353becc617ebc2831802a0b7a9a0a583eca2b58003003782",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000009",
        "block_index": 9,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "You know all those skills your baby has been perfecting? Of course you do, but the doctor will want to see them, too — or if baby’s not in the mood to perform, to hear about them from you. Some 9-month milestones include:",
        "text_sha256": "b7e32f283768482146719cacabdebe7b2fe58c1deb9e09b7e5579dc575193e14",
        "word_count": 43
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000010",
        "block_index": 10,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "• Getting into a sitting position and sitting unassisted",
        "text_sha256": "ab6f6d9206dc140f3c9426402b7aa364b19a0cd6d0927d8a34a84155379c93ab",
        "word_count": 9
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000011",
        "block_index": 11,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "• Crawling",
        "text_sha256": "7c011c001e08a2c8cd1c3d504ae4e661cd07ddc291e1ccdc00991634029341e3",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000012",
        "block_index": 12,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "• Pulling up to stand or standing holding onto someone/something",
        "text_sha256": "e1c687a23034742258a1facf36805ad561edcfed388cd5ef6d2970fe785b22f9",
        "word_count": 10
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000013",
        "block_index": 13,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "• Working to get a toy that’s out of reach and objecting if you take a toy away",
        "text_sha256": "68379ecdecffe5fdc313709cee95f38512fe7f881f2dc4081d74405e0d38fe9a",
        "word_count": 18
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000014",
        "block_index": 14,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "• Responding to her name",
        "text_sha256": "18257576bad2256af040117469d4e78b9f33b3b9fb69728a6c5f5aa1e882d038",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000015",
        "block_index": 15,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "• Laughing, squealing with delight",
        "text_sha256": "0e340dd3b1ef348d2248584d7f888f5437c96fa7bd6023d729431d218f0d852d",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000016",
        "block_index": 16,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "• Copying sounds and gestures",
        "text_sha256": "70a43db26d96deac8939f3403dd8f8e479fd1cfd11b6d0fcaf64f4198a47e3b6",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000017",
        "block_index": 17,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "• Pointing and using other gestures to communicate",
        "text_sha256": "df0fd7aac456d3cb33936c5300b37608d23dc847455f01c9fb56e7333c1f187a",
        "word_count": 8
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000018",
        "block_index": 18,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "• Following your gaze when you look away",
        "text_sha256": "79cbd60d9fb33e37b356d72d4ae9a30bdf1c4670a82cf5b17525b96ff8076557",
        "word_count": 8
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000019",
        "block_index": 19,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "• Saying \"Dada\" or \"Mama\" without meaning (or maybe even with!)",
        "text_sha256": "9ff83b4c6c92e96b90e6650609d482bcf53e850397401cb3a88b677e1108a84e",
        "word_count": 11
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000020",
        "block_index": 20,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "As always, there is a wide range of normal when it comes to baby development. Still, if you have any concerns, ask the doctor.",
        "text_sha256": "6c61170e6436035e579082876ae95c68cd99aebc683b842df32b098d98c36255",
        "word_count": 24
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000021",
        "block_index": 21,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Ask too if your baby doesn’t respond to her own name or recognize familiar people , doesn’t babble or make back-and-forth sounds, gestures or eye contact, doesn’t look where you point, doesn’t sit with help, or doesn’t transfer toys from one hand to the other.",
        "text_sha256": "622da7647a4415e6183f7ef78e7c701738d6219109c6859ae96a82aa8c1b66b3",
        "word_count": 45
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000022",
        "block_index": 22,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "9-month shots",
        "text_sha256": "0e403c50cf4ef89afaafcaf8851a76306e025551602ae7b0be054a89e19b8ec0",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000023",
        "block_index": 23,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Unless your baby has some catching up to do, or flu season is starting and she hasn’t received her two doses of this year's influenza vaccine , there likely won’t be any shots this time.",
        "text_sha256": "cf1564efcf237a5c576bd2ef4ed3bf7b4b2c05b52c3d307b3bf07cd7af7a5a1b",
        "word_count": 35
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000024",
        "block_index": 24,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Questions to ask your doctor",
        "text_sha256": "1ba32d8c91a61b5d7848063504ef84e35b945b3364dd3c17a5fc4cd6cf57d882",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000025",
        "block_index": 25,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Have you noticed any changes in your little one’s sleep patterns? (And just when you thought you could count on a schedule!) Sleep regression is common in months 8 to 10. Several factors may be standing in your baby’s way of getting the solid sleep she needs, including that compulsion to stand, even in bed, and practice other exciting skills.",
        "text_sha256": "ed14255b9f6255e0143e39ba1f80abe1b86aea9cbfe59c75f54e20efa2c4ce32",
        "word_count": 60
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000026",
        "block_index": 26,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Have questions about sleep regression, feeding, milestones or anything else? Now’s the time to ask:",
        "text_sha256": "49f142ee9066d287e80ccf9bc6795402de8ca41e409c62407475890bf1d454d9",
        "word_count": 15
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000027",
        "block_index": 27,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "How do I know if my baby is getting enough sleep?",
        "text_sha256": "8ac555d20637223dfbf9260a01fc0f3167aa692a0cd3143af788ff66c90f3620",
        "word_count": 11
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000028",
        "block_index": 28,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "My baby is starting to get super clingy around strangers. Is that normal?",
        "text_sha256": "f8563dbb3f9cd3f475b4d884ef01dedf0d64c9841f633d952645c76227c1efd8",
        "word_count": 13
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000029",
        "block_index": 29,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Is it time for finger foods ? Which finger foods are safe to start with?",
        "text_sha256": "fdc0422e33dd9639a3dbc5edb89df0838a5885b6e6fbc96717c34abd81d619ba",
        "word_count": 15
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000030",
        "block_index": 30,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "How do I take care of my baby’s teeth ?",
        "text_sha256": "2f8bba8bb610e97514b084bade758777e57bd3f5805d4c1c6ed80399d96cb4eb",
        "word_count": 10
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000031",
        "block_index": 31,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Should I teach my baby sign language ?",
        "text_sha256": "3919706e6019f7983f5ec19b588015f068ca2b5511c676e7726ae7ebe01a45f4",
        "word_count": 8
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000032",
        "block_index": 32,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "My baby isn’t pulling up yet. Should I be worried?",
        "text_sha256": "9841a11d9d44000019b8cdb811cf782b87f8b9f717e6b01851fb2aec42a4514b",
        "word_count": 10
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000033",
        "block_index": 33,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Are there any games, toys or activities I should introduce to help my baby learn?",
        "text_sha256": "4cfdeab0feecf5ab491295e200772824770bb77e7f2b376ac207708fa0c1073d",
        "word_count": 15
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000034",
        "block_index": 34,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Can I let my baby watch TV ?",
        "text_sha256": "c03ecc3c479884366b7db051d53f4f6cf506b71333f29cfb292c4ebe791e46e0",
        "word_count": 8
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000035",
        "block_index": 35,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Don't forget to schedule your next doctor's appointment before you leave, which will be the 12-month well-baby visit .",
        "text_sha256": "5558f9d33a6cba73bac1924aa16cadf21c23a3c680c1f37e26072ae234428290",
        "word_count": 19
      }
    ],
    "content_word_count": 603,
    "heading_count": 5
  },
  "title": "The 9-Month Well-Baby Doctor's Visit",
